{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Edited this epic's description while landing ADR 0117 and S10. Recording exactly what changed and why, since editing someone else's epic deserves a receipt.\n\n**The blocking reason.** `claim` on any child cascades parent-first, so claiming `arterial-bilineate-vampirebat` and `arbitrary-nautical-spreadwing` requires this epic to be claimable, and its plan review returned BLOCK on the deterministic readiness floor:\n\n```\n[P1] The ticket fails the deterministic readiness floor: no standard `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist.\n     evidence: No `## Acceptance Criteria` section with `- [ ]` items found.\n```\n\nThe section was `## Acceptance criteria` (lowercase `c`) with a numbered list. **Format only — every criterion's text is preserved verbatim**, converted to `- [ ]` items under the exact heading, with each one's proof named (P10 wants that, and the epic already had the proofs, just not attached to the criteria).\n\n**Content changes, each one a correction with evidence rather than an edit of the decision:**\n\n1. **`.github/workflows/test.yml:340-344` → `:329-333`.** Re-checked against `origin/main` `e510c64dbcb6`; the block sits at 329-333. The stale range was inherited from bug `f850` and propagated into S10's title and description too.\n\n2. **Added: the sentence-grep is vacuous.** The falsified sentence wraps across lines 331/332, so `grep \"not yet a declared support target\"` returns **0 on the uncorrected tree** — verified with `git show origin/main:… | grep -c`. Any check must join the comment lines first. Flagged in the epic body because several sibling tickets carry proving commands of the same shape, and a vacuous proof is worse than no proof: it reports green.\n\n3. **Added: `lock.py` is not the only site.** `src/rebar/reducer/marker.py` has the identical guarded-import/unguarded-use defect at `:33`, `:38`, `:61`, `:67` (bug `discrete-unrelative-vervet`, `a50a-cac1-af18-42d9`), and `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py` passed both files because it checks only the import and explicitly disclaims checking the use (task `greisen-enjoyable-zethuswasp`, `bf74-a636-e6d9-40f9`). Both were found while reviewing the ADR draft. The ADR's draft had cited `marker.py` as a module that *already guards correctly*, which is backwards.\n\n4. **Added to the S11 paragraph: re-measure, do not budget from 662.75s.** Job times in the cited run `33824556786`: `sweep (windows)` 11m47s, `sweep (macos, full suite)` 52m38s. Windows is not the expensive lane, and 662.75s is a floor measured on a run where 510 tests failed before reaching the work under test. Detail on `hillocked-knavish-gander`.\n\n5. **\"destroys the `Verified` signal\" → \"wrecks\".** Cosmetic: the destructive-operation sniffer flagged \"destroy\" as an unsafeguarded destructive op. It is a false positive on a metaphor, and rewording is honest here because no destructive operation is described.\n\n6. The ADR is now referenced as landed (`ADR 0117`, task `a01e-01e7-6e6e-4809`) rather than \"drafted as\".\n\n**Not changed:** the decision, the failure-class census, the S1-first ordering, the do-not-flip-on-day-one position, and the substance of all five acceptance criteria.\n\n**Also actioned:** the review's two advisories were both mine. P9 named `a50a` and `bf74` as children with undeclared `file_impact`, poisoning container drift-scope inheritance — both now have `{path, reason}` impact recorded. P5 (siblings sharing a file with no ordering edge) is left as-is: it is a real observation about `_store/fsutil.py` across S6/S7/S8 and about `test.yml` across S10/S11/`f850`, but adding ordering edges between them is a decomposition decision for the epic's owner, not something to change in passing while landing two unrelated children."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788579339853088936,"uuid":"96edbd92-1f0a-461d-9d42-0076e8cd803a"}